  "subject": "A young Irish priest posted to a Taigi-speaking parish in rural Changhua keeps getting his tones wrong, asking the lunch table to pick up their pigs (豬) instead of chopsticks (箸), until the front-pew old ladies adopt his slips as parish slang.",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien Irish traditional session folk, lively jig-time pub singalong. Tin whistle playing an ornamented lead tune with cuts and rolls; fiddle doubling the tune with open-string drones and bowed triplets; bodhran with a steady tipper pulse and rim clicks; DADGAD acoustic guitar in a driving open-string strum; tenor banjo plectrum triplets doubling the tune. Live pub-session mix, room ambience, dry hearty vocal. Male baritone-tenor, hearty open voice with a storyteller's grin, clearly sung melody. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 112 BPM, D major. Rowdy-warm, teasing, affectionate pub singalong. No rap, no drum machine, no electric guitar, no autotune, no synth pads.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n愛爾蘭來的 少年神父\n派來彰化 一間小教堂\n食飯進前 我欲講祈禱\n煞講出 一句大代誌\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n我講 逐家來攑豬\n老歲仔人 笑甲趴落去\n\n[Chorus]\n攑豬 攑豬 逐家攑豬\n箸仔 豬仔 我攏袂分\n頭排阿嬤 笑甲流目屎\n講神父 你閣來一擺\n\n[Verse]\n禮拜日 我講聖經\n講著牧羊人 牽羊仔轉來\n煞講成 牧豬人\n阿公點頭 講嘛通\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n後來彼群阿嬤 看見我\n就問 今仔日 攑豬無\n\n[Chorus]\n攑豬 攑豬 逐家攑豬\n聲調 我攏講甲歪去\n頭排阿嬤 笑甲流目屎\n講神父 你真正古錐\n\n[Verse]\n食飯進前 阿嬤逐擺\n先喝攑豬 才開動\n囡仔嘛學 會曉\n我的聲調 猶原歪歪\n\n[Bridge]\n愛爾蘭的老母 寫批來\n問我 豬仔 有照顧無\n\n[Chorus]\n攑豬 攑豬 逐家攑豬\n這句話 已經是咱的\n頭排阿嬤 笑甲流目屎\n神父你 毋免閣改啊\n\n[Outro]\n攑豬 攑豬\n食飯囉 逐家來",
